hi i'm evan carmichael and today i want  to do something a little bit different  usually i do profiles of famous  entrepreneurs and the top lessons you  can learn from their success  or i'm answering a question for one of  my readers today i want to share a  little bit about my story  and how i became an entrepreneur as well  as a program that really helped give me  the confidence to start my business  in the top three lessons that i learned  from that program i hope you enjoy okay  so here's a little bit about my story  i've been an entrepreneur as long as i  can remember the first  memory that i have to be an entrepreneur  is when i was five years old  i convinced my three-year-old little  sister to draw some pictures with me  with crayon  and then we went door-to-door trying to  sell it and we made our first  sale to our neighbor for 10 cents and  i've been an entrepreneur ever since  most of the business that i had early on  didn't go anywhere  baseball card businesses you know i made  a little bit of money extra spending  money but  i weren't really businesses it wasn't  until high school where  i joined a program called junior  achievement that really gave me the  confidence to become an entrepreneur  and what junior achievement is is they  have 40 kids that they get into an  after-school program  called the company program and they  launch their own company  and you have to come up with a product  idea you have to elect  a president and vice president you have  to do a business plan you have to raise  capital  basically all the things that you have  to do to run the real business but  you're in high school  and you've got some mentors from  different companies to help guide you  along the way  and so junior treatment really gave me a  lot of the confidence that i needed to  start my business  when i got to university i remember not  having anything about entrepreneurship  until i got to a fourth year course and  in that class  i had already done most of the stuff  that they were teaching in my junior  achievement program when i was already  running my business  so i really give junior treatment a lot  of the credit to me wanting to start my  own business and to the success that  i've had  as an entrepreneur and so i thought i  would share the top three lessons that  i've learned from my experience with  junior achievement  that have helped me grow my business  so the first lesson that i learned was  you have to sell  i was in junior achievement for three  years and some years we had  really good products but bad sales  people on our team  and we didn't really go anywhere with  our company and in other years we had  not so great products no decent products  gift baskets these aren't high-tech  products it's high school  but we had a really good sales team and  we were a lot more successful  and selling isn't really a skill that  they teach you in school but it is a  really vital  life skill that you need to be  successful as an entrepreneur and  as even a professional and so i really  credit junior achievement for giving me  that skill but you have to really think  about in your organization  selling you need everybody to know how  to sell in order for your company to get  to that next level of success  the second thing i learned from june  achievement is get big corporate orders  when we first started we tried to sell  to our friends and our family and  basically every  everybody that we knew who would you  know maybe we could guilt into buying  one of our products  then we quickly discovered that we were  out of friends and family to be able to  sell our stuff too  and sales dried up so we had to figure  out other ways to vote and  and get orders and my most successful  year of junior achievement was when we  were able to get  a big corporate company to make bigger  purchases and so we had fewer clients  but  they made a lot more purchases and it  was an ongoing type of transaction  so with your own business something i  still think about today a lot of people  are struggling trying to sell one-off  deals to customers who may not come back  or maybe a long time before they come  back again  and it's really time consuming but if  you can go and get bigger orders  that are more dollars for you and could  be an ongoing type of deal as well  it's much more profitable for your  business  the third thing i learned from junior  achievement is get everyone involved  in a junior achievement company you  might have 40 high school kids in the  program  and there's only so many management  positions once you let your president  and all your vice presidents everybody  else are just workers in the company  and it's really important that you make  them feel involved and and  an important part of the company or  they're going to leave the company and  it's just going to be the management  team that's left  and that's important lesson for your own  business you might be by yourself now  you might have a couple people around  you  and you're if you're the founder of the  business you're going to care way more  than everybody else  but you want to make sure that everybody  does feel like they're attached to the  company and they feel that they're  important they feel like what they're  giving  is a meaningful contribution and they're  happy about what they're doing with your  company  the more you can make it feel like  employees are really happy with what  they're doing and that what they're  doing is really important  the more likely you're going to get  better workers you're going to retain  them and your company is going to grow  so junior achievement helps over 250 000  students here in canada and many many  more around the world  wherever you are there's probably a  local june achievement chapter close to  you  and i encourage you to check it out and  get involved and be a mentor  to the new up and coming generation of  student entrepreneurs  so that's it for today thank you for  joining me for this video if you enjoyed  the video please give it a thumbs up  i'd also love to hear your thoughts and  feedback if you want to leave a comment  below and stay tuned for the next  episode  you
 

